<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>邻里相处 on 编程那些事儿</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E9%82%BB%E9%87%8C%E7%9B%B8%E5%A4%84/</link><description>Recent content in 邻里相处 on 编程那些事儿</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:31:03 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E9%82%BB%E9%87%8C%E7%9B%B8%E5%A4%84/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>邻里相处</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/life/neighbors/</link><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:40:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/life/neighbors/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;在美国住公寓或独栋房，跟邻居的关系有个很微妙的平衡：&lt;strong&gt;既要客气到能互相帮忙，又要保持距离不越界&lt;/strong&gt;。中国人习惯的&amp;quot;远亲不如近邻&amp;quot;（随时串门、借东西不问、有事直接敲门）在美国会显得过度亲近；反过来，完全不打招呼、电梯里低头看手机，又会被认为冷漠。&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>